  "prefLabel": "Plc 1104.01 Qualifications for Initial Practitioner Licensure",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Plc 1104.01 Qualifications for Initial Practitioner Licensure. As required by RSA 328-H:8, I, to qualify for initial licensure as a practitioner, an individual shall:\n\n(a) Be at least 18 years of age as of the date of application;\n\n(b) Hold a current certificate from a national certifying agency; and\n\n(c) Not have been convicted in New Hampshire or in any other jurisdiction of any crime involving violence inflicted on a person or threatened against a person, or any sexually-related crime.\n\nSource. #14444, eff 1-26-26, EXPIRES: 1-26-36",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/plc1100.html"
